ry hurts Ford, and any final polls or early-vote data could move the race in either direction.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["Incumbent Joe Lombardo (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Nevada's governor race sits at the center of the 2026 map: Republican incumbent Joe Lombardo seeks a second term against Democrat Aaron Ford, with independent Danielle Ford also on the ballot. The state's near-even partisan lean and a Democratic-tilted national environment pull in opposite directions, and seven of eight professional ratings call the race a Tossup, with Inside Elections the lone outlier tilting toward Lombardo.\n\nPolls through mid-October show a remarkably tight contest, with Lombardo ahead by about a point and many voters still undecided. Prediction markets diverge from the surveys, pricing Ford as a modest favorite at 66-69 percent, likely reflecting the anti-Trump climate and Democratic mobilization, including a Culinary Union rally with Kamala Harris. Ford also faces questions over past clemency votes. The outcome should be decided at the margins, with late-breaking voters decisive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4762, "margin": -0.32}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.447, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4885, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4837, "margin": -0.4}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4293, "margin": -0.7}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4243, "margin": -0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4798, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4823, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4769, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4774, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4597, "margin": -0.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.5079, "margin": -0.2}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.5047, "margin": -0.2}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.4683, "margin": -0.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.4673, "margin": -0.2}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem